        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): use Buffer.byteLength for JSON string byte-limit fast-path guard",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`jsonStringByteLengthUpToLimit` used `value.length` (UTF-16 code units) as a fast-path estimate. For CJK text this underestimates UTF-8 byte count by up to 3x, so the guard incorrectly passes strings that should bail early — triggering unnecessary `JSON.stringify` allocations.\n\nThe first fix (#106402 original) replaced the guard entirely with `Buffer.byteLength`, which fixed CJK accuracy but made oversized ASCII strings perform an O(n) scan instead of the original O(1) bailout.\n\nThis revision preserves both: the O(1) lower-bound guard catches clearly oversized strings instantly, then the O(n) UTF-8 guard catches the remaining CJK/emoji cases.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo-layer guard:\n\n1. `value.length + 2 > remainingBytes` — O(1), catches oversized ASCII immediately\n2. `Buffer.byteLength(value, \"utf8\") + 2 > remainingBytes` — O(n), catches CJK/emoji that passed the first guard\n3. `jsonUtf8BytesOrInfinity(value)` — fallback, accurate but expensive\n\nASCII behaviour is unchanged (`byteLength == length` for ASCII, so both guards agree). CJK strings that pass the O(1) guard still get the accurate UTF-8 check.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- No behavioural change for callers (`session-tool-result-guard`, `worker-environments/inference`, `tool-result-middleware`)\n- Oversized ASCII bailout restored to O(1)\n- CJK strings correctly bail without JSON.stringify allocation\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Two-layer guard correctness** (all three scenarios produce identical results):\n\n```\nOversized ASCII (50k chars, budget 8192):\n  O(1) guard: 50_002 > budget → bail immediately\n  result: { bytes: 8193, complete: false }  ← same as before\n\nCJK content (3k 中 chars, budget 8192):\n  O(1) guard: 3_002 ≯ 8_183 → falls through\n  O(n) guard: 9_002 > 8_183 → bail\n  result: { bytes: 8193, complete: false }  ← same as before\n\nFitting strings:\n  Both guards pass → jsonUtf8BytesOrInfinity → accurate count\n```\n\n**Unit tests**:\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/json-utf8-bytes.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/session-tool-result-guard.test.ts \\\n  src/gateway/worker-environments/inference.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/harness/tool-result-middleware.test.ts\n```\n\n```\nTest Files  6 passed (6)\n     Tests  106 passed (106)\n```\n\nThree new regression tests:\n- CJK bailout: 3,000 `\"中\"` chars pass O(1) guard, caught by Buffer.byteLength\n- ASCII fast-path: 50,000 `\"x\"` chars bail at O(1) guard\n- Unicode under limit: emoji strings within budget complete accurately\n\n**Diff**: 2 files, +22/-3. No pnpm-lock.yaml. Branch from upstream/main.\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
        "branch": "fix/json-utf8-byte-length-guard",
